From: Tobias Fischer <tobias.fischer@qut.edu.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Fix build against Eigen 5

Two unrelated problems show up when building DART 6.12 against Eigen 5:

* find_package(Eigen3 3.3.4 REQUIRED CONFIG) fails because Eigen 5's
  package version file only considers a request compatible when the
  requested major version matches the installed one, so the 5.x config
  file is rejected for a 3.3.4 request.
* Eigen 5 no longer includes <cassert> transitively, so the translation
  units that relied on getting assert() from an Eigen header fail with
  "use of undeclared identifier 'assert'".

diff --git a/cmake/DARTFindEigen3.cmake b/cmake/DARTFindEigen3.cmake
index e1acc08..bd51b5d 100644
--- a/cmake/DARTFindEigen3.cmake
+++ b/cmake/DARTFindEigen3.cmake
@@ -6,5 +6,15 @@
 #
 # This file is provided under the "BSD-style" License
 
-find_package(Eigen3 3.3.4 REQUIRED CONFIG)
+# Don't pass the minimum version to find_package(): the package version file
+# shipped by Eigen 5 only accepts requests for the major version it provides,
+# so asking for 3.3.4 makes the 5.x config file be rejected. Find whatever
+# version is installed and check the lower bound afterwards instead.
+find_package(Eigen3 REQUIRED CONFIG)
+
+if(Eigen3_VERSION AND Eigen3_VERSION VERSION_LESS 3.3.4)
+  message(FATAL_ERROR
+    "Eigen3 3.3.4 or greater is required, but found ${Eigen3_VERSION}."
+  )
+endif()
 
